## 3. How to Use This (Usage Guide)

### Step 1: Run the Default Campus Route
Open PowerShell or your terminal in `ai-mini-pjt` and run:
```powershell
.\.venv\Scripts\python.exe main.py
```
*(Routes from Campus Main Entrance Gate to Sports Ground & Athletics Field).*

---

### Step 2: Route Between Any Two Campus Buildings
Use the `--start` and `--target` arguments with any landmark from [`data/landmarks.json`](file:///c:/Users/giric/Desktop/project/ai-mini-pjt/data/landmarks.json):

```powershell
.\.venv\Scripts\python.exe main.py --start MITS_HOSTEL_B --target MITS_HOSTEL_G
```

#### Available Landmark Identifiers:
| Landmark ID | Building / Facility Name | Category |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| `MITS_MAIN_GATE` | Campus Main Entrance Gate | Entrance |
| `MITS_LIB` | Central Library | Academic |
| `MITS_ADMIN` | Administrative Headquarters | Administration |
| `MITS_CSE` | Computer Science & Engineering Block | Academic |
| `MITS_ECE` | Electronics & Electrical Engineering Block | Academic |
| `MITS_HOSTEL_B` | Boys Hostel Complex | Residential |
| `MITS_HOSTEL_G` | Girls Hostel Complex | Residential |
| `MITS_SPORTS` | Sports Ground & Athletics Field | Sports |
| `MITS_CANTEEN` | Campus Cafeteria & Student Center | Amenity |
| `MITS_AUDITORIUM`| University Auditorium | Facility |

---

### Step 3: Switch Network Modes (Walk vs Drive)
* **Pedestrian walkway mode (default):**
  ```powershell
  .\.venv\Scripts\python.exe main.py --start MITS_MAIN_GATE --target MITS_LIB --mode walk
  ```
* **Motorized vehicle road network:**
  ```powershell
  .\.venv\Scripts\python.exe main.py --start MITS_MAIN_GATE --target MITS_CSE --mode drive
  ```

---

### Step 4: Run Faster Without Generating Maps
For terminal-only benchmarking without regenerating the HTML and PNG visual files:
```powershell
.\.venv\Scripts\python.exe main.py --start MITS_HOSTEL_B --target MITS_SPORTS --no-viz
```

